    "sections" : [
      {
        "executes" : false,
        "heading" : "When to invoke",
        "line" : 21,
        "lines" : [
          "\"rotate credentials\"",
          "\"rotate stale credentials\"",
          "\"run the credential rotation pass\"",
          "This is meant to run unattended on a schedule, not only when a human asks",
          "for it — treat a manual invocation as a spot-check, not the primary trigger"
        ],
        "role" : "reference"
      },
      {
        "executes" : true,
        "heading" : "Workflow",
        "line" : 29,
        "lines" : [
          "fetch active credentials",
          "Check: any credentials whose status is \"active\"",
          "for each credential:",
          "wait 5 minutes",
          "until the credential is fresh,",
          "rotate a credential",
          "Emit: \"credential rotation pass complete\""
        ],
        "role" : "procedure"
      },
      {
        "executes" : false,
        "heading" : "Anti-Patterns",
        "line" : 38,
        "lines" : [
          "Don't rotate a credential once and move on without checking whether the",
          "provider actually applied the rotation — the retry loop exists because a",
          "single rotation call isn't proof of a fresh credential",
          "Don't skip the wait between attempts to \"save time.\" The identity",
          "provider needs that window to propagate the new secret; rotating again",
          "immediately just races the same in-flight change"
        ],
        "role" : "reference"
      },
      {
        "executes" : true,
        "heading" : "Guarantees",
        "line" : 46,
        "lines" : [
          "make sure no credentials whose status is \"active\" and whose use count is more than its use limit"
        ],
        "role" : "invariants"
      },
      {
        "executes" : false,
        "heading" : "Report shape",
        "line" : 49,
        "lines" : [
          "The receipt confirms every active credential is fresh at the end of the",
          "pass, or names which ones are still cycling if the provider is slow to",
          "confirm"
        ],
        "role" : "template"
      }
    ],
    "triggers" : "\"rotate credentials\"\n\"rotate stale credentials\"\n\"run the credential rotation pass\""
